## Findings

- **[P1] TTS cache ignores provider version and options.** The cache key only hashes provider ID, text, voice, and speed. Because `_step_tts` enables this cache, changing model, blend, language, provider settings, or manifest version can return the previous waveform before the provider is invoked. Workflow fingerprints also omit manifest version. Include normalized effective options and provider version in both layers. [dispatch.py:220](D:/@Workspace/@Development/@Scripts/@Python/ScriptToScene-Studio-V2/studio/tts/dispatch.py:220), [scheduler.py:686](D:/@Workspace/@Development/@Scripts/@Python/ScriptToScene-Studio-V2/studio/workflows/scheduler.py:686)

- **[P1] Multi-voice generation bypasses the selected provider.** `/api/tts/generate-multivoice` accepts no provider and unconditionally loads Kokoro. With Inworld selected, Inworld voices are rejected or the action silently generates Kokoro audio. This contradicts the Phase 15 requirement that legacy TTS routes work through both providers. [routes.py:937](D:/@Workspace/@Development/@Scripts/@Python/ScriptToScene-Studio-V2/studio/tts/routes.py:937), [routes.py:1067](D:/@Workspace/@Development/@Scripts/@Python/ScriptToScene-Studio-V2/studio/tts/routes.py:1067)

- **[P1] Cloud generation still requires downloading Kokoro.** The legacy TTS page unconditionally checks `modelReady` and calls the hardcoded Kokoro download endpoint before normal generation. On a clean Inworld-only installation, cloud TTS is blocked by an unrelated local-model download. Gate this behavior on the selected provider’s `model_download` capability. [useTts.js:328](D:/@Workspace/@Development/@Scripts/@Python/ScriptToScene-Studio-V2/frontend/src/features/tts/composables/useTts.js:328)

- **[P1] Unexpected streaming errors are exposed verbatim.** A third-party streaming provider throwing a normal exception has `str(e)` sent directly in the SSE response, bypassing the provider boundary’s redaction contract. Exceptions can disclose credentials, URLs, paths, or response bodies. Wrap unknown exceptions using the shared safe provider-error mapping. [routes.py:701](D:/@Workspace/@Development/@Scripts/@Python/ScriptToScene-Studio-V2/studio/tts/routes.py:701)

- **[P2] Pipeline voice routing remains limited to two concrete providers.** The updated composable explicitly fetches Kokoro and Inworld catalogs, then treats every provider other than Inworld as Kokoro. A fixture or plugin provider therefore receives Kokoro voices, failing the “another provider without UI edits” criterion and leaving P37–P39 incomplete. Load voices by the active provider ID and store drafts per provider dynamically. [usePipelineForm.js:81](D:/@Workspace/@Development/@Scripts/@Python/ScriptToScene-Studio-V2/frontend/src/features/pipeline/composables/usePipelineForm.js:81), [usePipelineForm.js:112](D:/@Workspace/@Development/@Scripts/@Python/ScriptToScene-Studio-V2/frontend/src/features/pipeline/composables/usePipelineForm.js:112)

